<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Richard Nixon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1913">1913</a>–<a href="/years/1994">1994</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Richard M. Nixon</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Richard Nixon was the 37th president of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, from 1969 to 1974. He withdrew American forces from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>, pursued détente with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> and, with Henry Kissinger, opened relations with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-republic-of-china">People's Republic of China</a>, visiting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a> in February 1972. Facing impeachment over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/watergate-scandal">Watergate scandal</a>, he became the only US president to resign.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/richard-nixon.jpg" alt="Richard Nixon" width="320" height="424" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Department of Defense. Department of the Army. Office of the Deputy Chief of Staff for Operations. U.S. Army Audiovis... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Richard_Nixon_presidential_portrait_(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
